id: pm-5uclvd
title: "GH-885: create-time close_reason_required recovery recommends an impossible different-command retry"
description: "GitHub issue #885 proves that when create requests a terminal status without closure evidence, close_reason_required lists only pm close examples against an item that was never created. The working create --resolution recovery is omitted, so the otherwise structured recovery bundle is not independently actionable."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",github-report,lifecycle,never-block,recovery
created_at: "2026-08-04T08:45:12.392Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T08:45:12.392Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Recovery examples and next steps are generated from the failing action contract and lead with the smallest valid same-command retry; CLI and SDK structured error contracts expose the same typed recovery with exact flag domains; A recovery-closure gate proves the refusal is actionable without help or source lookup and retains correct update/close-specific advice
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.3; default governance.require_close_reason; pm create --status closed without resolution
repro_steps: "Run pm --json create with a terminal status and no closure evidence; inspect examples, next_steps, and recovery fields"
expected_result: The recovery bundle names the valid same-command flag and produces a directly executable minimal retry
actual_result: Every example uses pm close against a nonexistent ID and next_steps omit --resolution
customer_impact: "Agents take an avoidable help/exploration loop, disable governance, or fall back to a non-atomic create-then-close sequence"
